    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/3/93179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "I think it's like a little bit of both. I still feel like I'm growing out of that myself. So sometimes I still feel like I'm feeling and I have like all this anxiety all the time and especially now, sometimes it feels like everyone's looking at you and no one is, you know? But now everyone actually is looking at me, and I'm like, oh my God. But I have started to just roll with it. And I'm like, guess what? I made a mistake, deal with it. Like, I'm trying, and you're not. So that's really the part that I've gotten to. It's like, yeah, I messed up. Who cares? Like, yeah, I said, and instead of butt on national television, deal with it. Like, deal with it because, you know, there's that famous Teddy Roosevelt quote. It's the person in the arena. They said, man, now is woman in the arena.",
