  {
    "episode_id": 93179,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/3/93179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "Great, because it's always, it's that so many times as women and as young women, we talk ourselves out of our best ideas. We talk ourselves out of running for office. We talk ourselves out of starting a business. And then we see somebody else do the very thing we told ourselves we couldn't do. And we're left with so much regret and envy. And so I always say, it goes like, go to where that envy is, because we won't build sisterhood unless we're living a life without regret. And that does mean that most of the time, it ain't gonna happen. But at least you don't have regrets.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Women and young women frequently doubt their own abilities and dismiss their best ideas.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Women often refrain from pursuing ambitious goals like running for office or starting a business due to self-doubt.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Seeing others succeed in areas one previously doubted oneself in leads to feelings of regret and envy.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Envy can serve as a signal for unfulfilled personal aspirations.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Living a life free of regret requires taking risks despite low odds of success.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The absence of regret is essential for building genuine sisterhood among women.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Self-doubt is a common psychological barrier specifically experienced by women and young women.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Regret is a meaningful emotional indicator of missed opportunities aligned with personal values.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "True sisterhood depends on authenticity and shared experiences of risk-taking rather than superficial solidarity.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Emotional states like envy should be interpreted as useful signals rather than dismissed as negative emotions.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Personal growth and empowerment require confronting fear and uncertainty even when outcomes are uncertain.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 93179,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/3/93179.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, absolutely. And oftentimes, the thing that you want to do or want to try is just, it's like a breadcrumb. You know, you may think that you may want something. I feel like we're in opposite positions because when I first graduated in college, it was my dream actually to do social enterprise work and to work with young people. in developing an educational venture and I tried and I fell on my face.",
