    "turn_text": "One of my favorite quotes right now, as I'm going through this book, is if life for one long grade school, girls would rule the world. And it's not, right? So what happens in the real world is that bravery matters. When you raise your hand for something that you don't fully understand, or you run for Congress, when people are telling you you have no chance of winning, when you have something that you've been dreaming about, but everyone tells you you can't do something. that's like in the real world what's gonna like really not only just find you success but find you joy and that's the other thing I would tell you we were talking about this it's like we're in such this success driven culture where we want one thing and then another thing and then another thing and we get that one thing get that A on that test win office start girls who code write a book and you're like oh this is what it feels like",
